;; T0.2 negative control — value-uniqueness premise (G1).
;;
;; The soak/staleness judgement treats a write's value as its global sequence
;; number, so the checker must refuse to conclude anything when that premise is
;; broken: here two write *invocations* carry value 3. Everything else passes —
;; the single quiet window [1.0s, 1.111s] has 12 all-:ok write completions
;; (ratio 1.00, judged), and there is no disruption at all, so the RTO gate is
;; vacuous. Only the premise gate fires:
;;   {:type :duplicate-values, :count 1, :sample {3 2}}
